# Environment variables

Configuration is read exclusively from environment variables (`src/config.ts`). Defaults below are the application defaults. The deployed values are set per environment in the system's gitops-app repo (`system.yaml`: a component's `env`, and `replicas`, `resources` under `instances.<env>`).

## Core

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | `{{ port }}` | HTTP port the service listens on. |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | pino level, any case: `TRACE`, `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR`, `FATAL`. Unknown values fall back to `INFO`. |
{%- if needs_observability %}

## Observability

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | unset | OTLP endpoint for traces; unset means tracing is off. |
| `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` | `{{ project_name }}` | Service name on traces. |
| `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED` | unset | `true` turns tracing off even with an endpoint. |
{%- endif %}
{%- if needs_database %}

## Database (PostgreSQL)

Set by the platform's `postgres` resource when the service declares `uses: [postgres]`; the defaults match `devbox run db-up`.

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `PGHOST` | `localhost` | Database host. |
| `PGPORT` | `5432` | Database port. |
| `PGDATABASE` | `{{ project_name | replace('-', '_') }}` | Database name. |
| `PGUSER` | `app` | Database user. |
| `PGPASSWORD` | unset | Database password (generated and injected from a Secret in the cluster, never committed; `db-up` needs none). |
{%- endif %}
